examples.question_text:
A circle has diameter $XY$ and centre $Z(2,1)$. One endpoint is $Y(5,-3)$. Find the coordinates of $X$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (2,1) circle[radius=25mm];
\draw[black] (-1,5)--(5,-3);
\fill[black] (-1,5) circle[radius=1.5pt];
\fill[black] (2,1) circle[radius=1.5pt];
\fill[black] (5,-3) circle[radius=1.5pt];
\path (-1,5) node[above left] {$X$};
\path (2,1) node[above right] {$Z(2,1)$};
\path (5,-3) node[below right] {$Y(5,-3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
